### Online Payments

Mollie's online payments suite provides businesses with flexible infrastructure to accept payments across channels and customer journeys. It covers everything from a fully hosted checkout experience to direct API integrations, standalone payment links, and automated recurring billing.

How it works

Merchants can accept payments through four main methods. The hosted checkout presents customers with a Mollie-managed payment page, reducing the PCI compliance burden on the merchant. The direct payment API gives developers full control to build native checkout experiences within their own environment. Payment links allow merchants to generate shareable URLs that lead directly to a payment page — useful for invoices, social commerce, or one-off requests. Recurring payments automate collection for subscriptions or instalments using stored mandates.

Product features and USPs

Hosted checkout — a pre-built, Mollie-managed payment page; fast to implement, PCI-friendly, and supports all major payment methods
Direct payment APIs — RESTful API integration giving full control over the payment UX and flow, suited to developers building custom checkout experiences
Payment links — shareable, no-code payment URLs that can be sent via email, SMS, WhatsApp, or embedded in invoices; no customer login or account required
Recurring payments — mandate-based automated billing supporting both fixed and variable amounts, built for subscription businesses and instalment plans
Multi-currency and localisation — accepts payments in multiple currencies with localised payment method display based on customer geography
Broad payment method coverage — supports cards (Visa, Mastercard, Amex), iDEAL, Bancontact, SEPA Direct Debit, PayPal, Apple Pay, Google Pay, Klarna, and more

Who it is for

Online payments is suited to any business that sells digitally — e-commerce retailers, SaaS companies, marketplaces, and service providers — regardless of technical resource, thanks to both no-code and full-API implementation paths.

