### In-Person Payments (POS or Point of Sale)

Mollie's in-person payments product extends Mollie's payment infrastructure into physical and hybrid retail environments. It allows merchants to accept face-to-face payments using smartphones or dedicated hardware, unified with their online Mollie account and reporting.

How it works

Merchants can accept in-person payments through three routes. Tap to Pay turns a compatible Android or iPhone into a contactless card reader with no additional hardware needed. PAX hardware terminals are purpose-built payment terminals supplied and managed through Mollie. POS software and SoftPOS solutions allow merchants to integrate Mollie's payment acceptance into their existing point-of-sale software stack.

Product features and USPs

Tap to Pay (Android) — turns any NFC-enabled Android device into a card reader using only the Mollie app; accepts contactless cards and digital wallets
Tap to Pay (iPhone) — Apple's native Tap to Pay capability integrated into the Mollie app; no card reader hardware required, fully compliant with Apple's security framework
Tap terminal — a lightweight, portable payment terminal with built-in 
4G and Wi-Fi, all-day battery, and drop- and splash-resistance; ships 
ready to use. Hardware cost: £45 (UK) / €95 (EU). Available on two 
plans — Pay as you go (no monthly fee, one terminal maximum) or Pro 
(monthly fee, includes one terminal licence). See Pricing section for 
full plan details and per-transaction rates.
PAX hardware terminals — certified payment terminals for merchants who prefer dedicated hardware; managed through Mollie with remote configuration capability
POS software integration — Mollie connects with third-party POS software used in retail and hospitality environments
SoftPOS — software-based point-of-sale functionality enabling payment acceptance on commercial off-the-shelf devices without proprietary hardware
Unified reporting — in-person and online transactions appear in the same Mollie Dashboard, giving a single view of revenue across channels
No separate merchant account — in-person payments run through the same Mollie account as online payments, simplifying reconciliation and settlement

Who it is for

In-person payments is suited to omnichannel retailers, hospitality businesses, market traders, pop-up operators, and any merchant who needs to accept face-to-face payments without investing in complex hardware infrastructure.

