### Omnichannel Payments 

Mollie's omnichannel offering unifies a merchant's online and in-person payments under a single Mollie account, so transactions, customers, payouts, and reporting are connected across every channel rather than split across separate systems. 

How it works 

Online and in-store payments run through the same Mollie account and Dashboard. Reconciliation is automated, customers are recognised wherever they pay, and revenue from web checkout and physical terminals appears in one consolidated view. Refunds can cross channels (e.g. an online order returned in-store), and all revenue settles into a single predictable payout. 

Product features and USPs 

Unified dashboard — real-time view of online revenue and physical terminal performance in one place 
Cross-channel refunds — customers can return online orders in-store, reducing manual admin 
Consolidated payouts — all channel revenue in one payout for simpler cash flow and reporting 
Remote terminal management — order, configure, and monitor devices across all locations 
One integration, every method — cards, wallets, local methods, gift cards, vouchers, payment links, and QR across online and physical stores 
Scalable POS suite — Tap to Pay, mobile terminals, and fixed kiosks, from pop-ups to permanent locations 
Broad ecosystem — connects with 350+ POS, commerce, and accounting platforms 
Single customer journey — one connected experience from online checkout to in-store, supporting loyalty and repeat revenue 

Who it is for 

Omnichannel payments suits retailers, hospitality businesses, and brands that sell both online and in physical locations and want a single, connected view of payments, customers, and settlement across channels. 

