### Invoicing
Mollie's invoicing product allows merchants to create and send invoices directly from within the Mollie platform, with payment collection built in. It removes the need for a separate invoicing tool by combining invoice generation and payment link functionality in a single workflow.

How it works

Merchants create invoices inside the Mollie Dashboard, specifying line items, amounts, and recipient details. Mollie generates the invoice and attaches a payment link, which the customer can use to pay directly online using their preferred payment method. Payment status updates automatically in the Dashboard once the invoice is settled.

Product features and USPs

Invoice creation — build and send professional invoices directly from the Mollie Dashboard without third-party invoicing software
Integrated payment collection — every invoice includes a Mollie-powered payment link, allowing customers to pay immediately via card, bank transfer, or other supported methods
Automatic status tracking — invoice and payment status updates in real time, reducing the need for manual follow-up
Payment method flexibility — customers can pay using any payment method supported by Mollie, not just bank transfer
No additional software needed — invoicing is embedded within the existing Mollie account and Dashboard, keeping workflows consolidated

Who it is for

Mollie's invoicing product is suited to freelancers, service businesses, B2B merchants, and SMEs who need a straightforward way to bill clients and collect payment — without managing separate invoicing software and payment collection tools.

More info:

Invoicing overview: https://www.mollie.com/products/invoicing

### Connect (Platform-based payments infrastructure layer)
Mollie Connect is Mollie's infrastructure layer for platforms, marketplaces, and networks that need to manage payments on behalf of multiple merchants or sub-merchants. It provides the tooling to embed payment acceptance, handle onboarding, route funds, and manage settlement at scale — without building a proprietary payments stack.

How it works

Platforms integrate with Mollie Connect via API to extend Mollie's payment infrastructure to their own merchant base. Mollie handles regulatory compliance, merchant onboarding (including KYC), and payment processing under a single integration. Platforms can control how funds flow between themselves and their sub-merchants through split payments and settlement routing logic.

Product features and USPs

SaaS platform payments — enables SaaS businesses to embed payment acceptance natively into their product, creating a revenue stream and reducing merchant churn
Marketplace payments — supports multi-party payment flows where funds are split between a marketplace operator and sellers, with Mollie handling compliance and disbursement
Franchise network payments — allows franchise operators to centralise payment infrastructure across franchise locations while maintaining individual merchant settlement
E-commerce platform integrations — pre-built integrations with major e-commerce platforms (WooCommerce, Magento, Shopify, etc.) for rapid merchant onboarding
Merchant onboarding and sub-merchant management — Mollie handles KYC and regulatory onboarding for sub-merchants, removing compliance burden from the platform
Split payments and settlement routing — configurable rules for how funds are divided and distributed between platform, marketplace operator, and individual merchants
Revenue share models — platforms can configure service fees or revenue share arrangements within the payment flow
Single API integration — one Mollie Connect integration supports all sub-merchants on the platform, rather than each merchant integrating independently

Who it is for

Connect is designed for SaaS companies, marketplace operators, franchise networks, and e-commerce platform providers who want to embed payments as a core part of their product offering and manage multiple merchants under a single payments infrastructure.

