### Mollie Capital 

Mollie Capital provides a lump-sum cash advance to eligible merchants. Repayment happens automatically as a fixed percentage deducted from the merchant's daily Mollie payment volume. There are no fixed monthly instalments — repayment naturally speeds up in busy periods and slows during quiet ones, matching the merchant's cash flow.

The advance comes with a single flat fee, calculated at the time of the offer. There is no compound interest, no early repayment penalty, and no hidden fees. The total repayment amount is known upfront.

Eligibility

Mollie Capital is available exclusively to merchants who already use Mollie as their payment provider. Eligibility is determined automatically using the merchant's Mollie payment history — no lengthy credit application, no traditional collateral. Eligible merchants see an offer directly in their Mollie Dashboard.

Product features and USPs

Fast access to capital — offers are generated automatically; funding typically arrives within 1–2 business days of signing
Revenue-based repayment — repayment scales with daily revenue, not a fixed calendar
Transparent, single fee — one factor rate applied upfront; total cost is visible before acceptance
No dilution or collateral — no equity stake, no property security required
Embedded in the Mollie Dashboard — merchants apply, sign, and track repayment without leaving Mollie
Renewable — once repaid, eligible merchants may receive a follow-on (top-up) offer
Powered by payment data — credit decisioning uses actual Mollie transaction history, not just credit bureau scores

Who it is for

Mollie Capital is suited for e-commerce businesses, retail merchants, and service providers who process card and online payments through Mollie and need working capital for inventory, marketing, hiring, or expansion — without the complexity or wait of a bank loan.

More info:

Capital overview: https://www.mollie.com/products/capital

### Business Accounts 

Mollie's Business Accounts product gives eligible merchants a dedicated business payment account held within the Mollie platform. It extends Mollie beyond payment processing into day-to-day business banking functionality, allowing merchants to hold, manage, and spend funds — all from within the same platform they use to accept payments.

